# Lofthus permanent deploy

Applies to every implementation task unless the user says `do not deploy`.

Branch: `integration-v2` only. Never merge `main` automatically.

## Definition of done

Not finished if it only works locally.

1. Preserve legitimate local work (no reset/discard of newer local commits).
2. Run relevant tests.
3. Run production build when frontend changed.
4. Commit completed changes.
5. `git push origin integration-v2`
6. Wait for deployment.
7. Verify the **public** version.

## Frontend

Repo: `sindrekolberg-cmyk/lofthus-web`

Canonical preview (always report this, never unique `*-xxxxx-genetic1` URLs):

https://lofthus-road-open-kontrollrom-uvvh-git-integration-v2-genetic1.vercel.app/

Vercel auto-deploys `integration-v2`. Localhost is not final QA.

## Backend

Repo: `sindrekolberg-cmyk/lofthus-road-open-kontrollrom`

Public API: https://lofthus-road-open-api.onrender.com

Render auto-deploys `integration-v2`. Push ≠ deployed. Probe the public API (e.g. new fields / `round_kicker`) until the new commit is live.

## Full-stack

Backend test → push backend → frontend test/build → push frontend → wait Render → wait Vercel → test canonical frontend against public API.

Do not declare success if the frontend expects an API Render has not deployed.

## Failure

If Vercel or Render fails: do not pretend done. Report what succeeded, what failed, latest commit, deploy status.

## Report shape

DONE / TESTS / DEPLOY (frontend SHA, backend SHA if relevant, Vercel, Render, canonical URL).
The user should normally need to do nothing manually.
